        "explanation": "Senator Schumer announces federal fire grants for Westchester County and highlights his role in pushing for additional funding, taking direct credit for the outcome."
      }
    ],
    "negative_clarification": "Credit-claiming does NOT occur when the senator discusses general policy positions, criticizes others, or provides commentary without tying their personal actions to a specific outcome. Statements that focus on broader issues, express opinions, or describe the work of others without claiming a direct role do not qualify as credit-claiming.",
